    "@value" : "The controlled vocabulary of payment instruments and rails, informed by ISO 20022 payment-type semantics."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Payment Instrument Scheme"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#paymentInstrumentSepaTransfer",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PaymentInstrument"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A euro-denominated credit transfer within the Single Euro Payments Area."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#paymentInstrumentScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "sepa-transfer"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "SEPA Transfer"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#paymentInstrumentWireTransfer",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PaymentInstrument"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An interbank credit transfer settled individually, such as Fedwire, CHAPS, or a cross-border SWIFT payment."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#paymentInstrumentScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "wire-transfer"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Wire Transfer"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#performedBy",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid179"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates an activity (a Process, an Event such as a log record, or any other CyberActivity) to the Agent that performed it, or a Plan to the Agent responsible for carrying it out."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "performedBy"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "On an execution, name the performer as observed. When the evidence shows only an identity, such as an account in an audit log, the performer is that DigitalIdentity, and the Agent behind it is reached through stonework:accountOf or stonework:attributedToAgent. When an identity may have been used by someone other than its holder, keep the identity as the performer and record the Agent believed responsible with stonework:attributedTo; an analyst who establishes the misuse records a stonework:Deviation. Who is expected to perform a Plan's Steps is given per Step, as Roles (stonework:performerRole)."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#performerRole",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Step"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Role"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#hadRole"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A Role whose holder is expected to perform this Step: the plan-side assignment of work, as in a BPMN lane."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "performerRole"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "If several Roles are given, a holder of any one of them may perform the Step; a requirement that two people act (dual control) is two Steps, linked by stonework:separatedFrom. An execution conforms when its performer, or the Agent its performer identity belongs to (stonework:accountOf, stonework:attributedToAgent), holds the Role through a stonework:RoleAssignment whose stonework:roleContext is the Plan's performer and which is in force (stonework:validFrom, stonework:validUntil) when the execution starts. Someone acting through a role holder's misused identity passes this check, which is why a misused identity is recorded as a stonework:Deviation."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#phishingResistant",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#AuthenticatorType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Whether an authenticator type is bound to the site it authenticates to, so that a phishing proxy relaying the sign-in can't use it."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "phishingResistant"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#phoneNumberOf",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PhoneNumber"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The Agent associated with this PhoneNumber. Inverse of stonework:hasPhoneNumber."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "phoneNumberOf"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#phoneValue",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PhoneNumber"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The phone number string in E.164 or local format."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "phoneValue"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#pid",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RuntimeProcess"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The process identifier assigned by the OS."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "pid"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#planFormat",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Plan"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The machine-readable format a Plan is also kept in, e.g. CACAO JSON for a playbook or BPMN for a business process."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "planFormat"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#planVersion",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Plan"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The version string of a Plan."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "planVersion"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A run follows the version of the Plan individual it is stonework:executionOf."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookFormat",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Playbook"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#planFormat"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated" : [ {
    "@type" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean",
    "@value" : "true"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The machine-readable format of the playbook (e.g. CACAO JSON, BPMN, YAML)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "playbookFormat"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Deprecated: use stonework:planFormat, which applies to every stonework:Plan."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeAttack",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Penetration testing or adversary emulation, or an adversary's own operation as reconstructed from intelligence. stonework:OperationPlan is this type."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "attack"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Attack"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeDetection",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Detecting a known security event or expected security-relevant activity, or threat hunting. stonework:DetectionPlan is this type."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "detection"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Detection"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeEngagement",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Denial, deception and other adversary engagement that raises the adversary's cost or lowers the value of its operations (see MITRE Engage)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "engagement"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Engagement"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeInvestigation",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Investigating what a security event, incident or other activity has affected. stonework:InvestigationPlan is this type."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "investigation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Investigation"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeMitigation",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Reducing or limiting the impact of an event or incident until it can be remediated. A stonework:ControlPlan is often this type."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "mitigation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Mitigation"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeNotification",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Notifying others and disseminating information or playbooks about an event, incident or threat."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "notification"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Notification"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypePrevention",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Preventing a known or expected event, incident or threat from occurring. A stonework:ControlPlan is often this type."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "prevention"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Prevention"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeRemediation",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PlaybookType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Returning affected systems to a known good state after an event or incident. A stonework:ControlPlan is often this type."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "remediation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Remediation"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookTypeScheme",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Playbook Type Scheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The controlled vocabulary of what a Plan is for, aligned with CACAO 2.0's playbook types."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Playbook Type Scheme"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playbookVersion",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Playbook"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#planVersion"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated" : [ {
    "@type" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean",
    "@value" : "true"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The version string of the playbook."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "playbookVersion"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Deprecated: use stonework:planVersion, which applies to every stonework:Plan."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#playsRole",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Role"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#propertyChainAxiom" : [ {
    "@list" : [ {
      "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#hasRoleAssignment"
    }, {
      "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole"
    } ]
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A context-free projection of a Role played by an entity."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "playsRole"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Use stonework:RoleAssignment with stonework:roleContext when the campaign, operation, organization, provenance, or time interval matters. The qualified pattern infers this direct projection through a property chain."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#port",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#NetworkService"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedShort"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The TCP/UDP port number on which the service listens."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "port"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#posesThreat",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid184"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Threat"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a ThreatActor or Campaign to the Threats they represent."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "posesThreat"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#postalCode",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Location"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The postal or ZIP code of the location."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "postalCode"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Step"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Step"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a Step to another Step that must occur before it within the same parent Behavior."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "precededByStep"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Deliberately distinct from stonework:precedes, whose domain and range are IntelligenceProduct (report-version succession) — an unrelated relationship. precededByStep expresses a graph that may contain cycles: an edge targeting an already-reached Step is a loop, not an error. A Step with several precededByStep values follows all of them; Steps with no precededByStep path between them are unordered and may be performed in parallel, so a dependency graph of precededByStep edges expresses parallel work without stonework:splitKind or stonework:joinKind. Use stonework:Transition instead when the edge itself needs a guard condition or other structure attached."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precedes",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#IntelligenceProduct"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#IntelligenceProduct"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Temporal succession of Information (v1 precedes v2 of a report)"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "precedes"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedLiteral",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Hypothesis"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The scalar value a Hypothesis predicts its stonework:predictsVariable will be bound to, once executed."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "predictedLiteral"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Mirrors stonework:boundToLiteral on the actual-result side; see stonework:predictedValue for predictions of an individual rather than a scalar."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Hypothesis"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The class a Hypothesis predicts its stonework:predictsVariable will be bound to an instance of, once executed."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "predictedType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Mirrors stonework:guardType on Transition. Exists because a Hypothesis is typically formed before the Variable's eventual value has been constructed — at prediction time there is usually no individual yet to name via stonework:predictedValue, only an expected class of outcome (e.g. 'this attempt will produce some stonework:SecurityCondition')."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Hypothesis"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The individual a Hypothesis predicts its stonework:predictsVariable will be bound to, once executed."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "predictedValue"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Mirrors stonework:boundTo on the actual-result side; usable only when a specific pre-existing individual is predicted. See stonework:predictedType for the more common case of predicting a class of outcome rather than a specific not-yet-constructed individual, and stonework:predictedLiteral for predictions of a scalar."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Hypothesis"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Variable"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The Variable whose eventual binding a Hypothesis is a prediction about."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "predictsVariable"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Because stonework:hasInputVariable/stonework:hasOutputVariable are declared on stonework:Behavior, and stonework:Step is itself a Behavior, a Hypothesis may predict a Variable declared at any level of a Step/Plan decomposition — a top-level Plan's overall outcome or a single Step's individual result — without a separate property per level."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityCritical",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PriorityLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Work immediately, ahead of everything else."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "critical"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Critical"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityHigh",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PriorityLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Work as soon as possible."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "high"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "High"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityLevelScheme",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Priority Level Scheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The controlled vocabulary of work priority levels."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Priority Level Scheme"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityLow",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PriorityLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Work when higher-priority matters allow."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "low"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Low"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityMedium",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#PriorityLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Work in the normal course."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#priorityLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "medium"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Medium"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#procedureFor",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Procedure"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Technique"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#implements"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a Procedure to the Technique it implements; a specialized form of stonework:implements for procedure-to-technique links."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "procedureFor"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#produces",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberActivity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberEntity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Links an executing CyberActivity to a CyberEntity it constructed or generated in the course of executing."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "produces"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "General-purpose construction/generation link — e.g. the CyberActivity realizing a Step is what actually constructs the value a Variable ends up stonework:boundTo, or a complex output artifact (a dataset, a report) that value refers to."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#producesReport",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid187"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid190"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a Process or Investigation to the intelligence product it generates."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "producesReport"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productName",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Product"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The canonical product name."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "productName"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeAIModel",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A trained machine learning or AI model distributed as a deployable artifact, subject to threats such as model poisoning, extraction, inversion, and adversarial evasion."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "ai-model"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "AI Model"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeApplication",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A software application designed to perform specific tasks for end users or other systems. Corresponds to CPE component type 'a'."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "application"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Application"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeContainerImage",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A packaged, layered filesystem image used to instantiate containers. Subject to threats including image tampering, malicious base layers, and registry poisoning."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "container-image"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Container Image"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeFirmware",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Software permanently programmed into a hardware device, typically stored in non-volatile memory and providing low-level control of the device. Corresponds to CPE component type 'o' when used in embedded contexts."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "firmware"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Firmware"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeHardware",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A physical computing device, component, or peripheral. Corresponds to CPE component type 'h'."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "hardware"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Hardware"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeLibrary",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A reusable collection of code, routines, or resources linked into applications or other software components, often a source of transitive vulnerabilities."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "library"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Library"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeOperatingSystem",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "System software that manages hardware resources and provides common services for application software. Corresponds to CPE component type 'o'."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "operating-system"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Operating System"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypePackage",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A distributable unit of software published to a package registry (e.g. npm, PyPI, Maven, NuGet). The primary unit of supply chain attack surface — distinct from Library in that a package has its own versioning, signing, provenance chain, and registry identity."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "package"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Package"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeSDK",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A software development kit providing tools, libraries, and APIs used to build applications for a specific platform or framework."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "sdk"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "SDK"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Product Type Scheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The controlled vocabulary of product functional categories."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Product Type Scheme"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeService",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A networked or cloud-hosted software capability consumed by other systems or users, such as a SaaS platform, API service, or managed infrastructure service."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#productTypeScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "service"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Service"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#protects",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid193"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid196"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a Countermeasure or ACL to the resource it protects."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "protects"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#provenanceOf",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Provenance"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid199"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a Provenance record to the IntelligenceProduct or QualifiedAssertion whose origin or evidentiary basis it documents."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "provenanceOf"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#publishedDate",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The date the item was first publicly published or disclosed."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "publishedDate"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Compatibility alias for dcterms:issued. Prefer dcterms:issued in newly authored data."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#purl",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#VersionedProduct"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The Package URL (PURL) identifying this software package version."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "purl"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#rawEntry",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Log"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The raw, unprocessed log line or record."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "rawEntry"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#redirectsTo",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#MailboxRule"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#EmailAddress"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An address a MailboxRule redirects the messages it selects to, keeping the original sender, so the recipient sees them as if sent directly."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "redirectsTo"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#references",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Generic reference from one entity to another. Use a more specific property where one exists."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "references"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#referencesMessage",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#EmailMessage"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#EmailMessage"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An earlier EmailMessage of the same thread, named by its Message-ID in the References header."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "referencesMessage"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#refersTo",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates an object, from an intelligence source or from evidence, to the canonical entity it refers to, such as an ATT&CK technique, a CVE, a malware family, or one of the organization's own assets or accounts, when the two are distinct individuals."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "refersTo"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Unlike owl:sameAs, it does not merge the two individuals' properties. Two STIX objects with different STIX IDs are different objects even when both describe T1059: stones:stixId is functional, so owl:sameAs between them is inconsistent. Unlike skos:exactMatch, it does not make either end a skos:Concept. Domain and range intentionally unset: any intelligence object can refer to any canonical entity. A link found by a heuristic, such as an identifier parsed from a name, should carry its method and confidence through a stonework:QualifiedAssertion or stonework:hasProvenance. The same holds for what evidence names: the resource a log or message gives a tenant, an account or a host refersTo the organization's own entity for it, such as a Plan Step's target, without merging the two. Neither symmetric nor transitive, so nothing follows from it unless an application follows it: an analyst can retract the link without retracting anything inferred from it, and competing links can stand side by side until one is judged."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#refines",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#AttackTechnique"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#AttackPattern"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates an AttackTechnique to a broader or more abstract AttackPattern that it specializes, enabling roll-up from operational techniques to pattern families."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "refines"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#regionCode",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Region"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The ISO 3166-2 region code (e.g. US-CA, GB-ENG)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "regionCode"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#registeredTo",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Infrastructure"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates infrastructure to the Agent recorded as its owner or registrant of record — the entity in whose name the resource is officially registered."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "registeredTo"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#registeredWith",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Infrastructure"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates infrastructure to the registrar, registry, or administrative authority through which the registration was processed or is maintained."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "registeredWith"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#registrationDate",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Domain"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The date and time when the domain was first registered."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "registrationDate"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Uses xsd:dateTime so source-native registration timestamps, including dns:registeredOn, can map without losing precision."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#registryKeyPath",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RegistryKey"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The full registry key path (e.g. HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\...)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "registryKeyPath"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#registryValueData",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RegistryValue"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The typed literal data stored in the registry value."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "registryValueData"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The broad literal range preserves string, numeric, multi-string, and binary-valued source representations. Use stonework:registryValueType to record the Windows registry type explicitly."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#registryValueName",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RegistryValue"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The name of the registry value."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "registryValueName"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#registryValueType",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RegistryValue"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The type of the registry value (e.g. REG_SZ, REG_DWORD, REG_BINARY)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "registryValueType"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedAttackPattern",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#AttackPattern"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates an entity to an AttackPattern representing the same underlying technique in a different framework shape, resolved from a shared technique identifier (e.g. a CAPEC entry and the MITRE ATT&CK technique it maps to, or a CWE weakness and the CAPEC pattern that exploits it)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "relatedAttackPattern"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Domain intentionally left unset: subjects include stonework:Weakness (CWE → CAPEC) and stonework:AttackPattern itself (CAPEC → ATT&CK). Materialized by joining a framework's technique-identifier literal (see stonework:relatedTechniqueIdentifier) against the ATT&CK technique's external reference. Framework ontologies declare their concrete property (e.g. capec:relatedAttackTechnique, cwe:relatedAttackPattern) as rdfs:subPropertyOf this."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberTechnique"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberTechnique"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a CyberTechnique to another related CyberTechnique via a cross-framework or cross-abstraction-level association."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "relatedTechnique"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "For technique-to-technique associations where both ends are already stonework:CyberTechnique individuals. Where the association instead crosses AttackPattern shapes (e.g. CWE weakness → CAPEC pattern, CAPEC pattern → ATT&CK technique), use stonework:relatedAttackPattern, whose domain is not restricted to CyberTechnique."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechniqueIdentifier",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A framework-native technique identifier string (e.g. a MITRE ATT&CK technique ID such as 'T1003.001') carried on an entity from another framework, both for provenance and as the join key used to materialize the corresponding stonework:relatedAttackPattern or stonework:mitigatesAttackPattern edge."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "relatedTechniqueIdentifier"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Domain intentionally left unset: populated on entities as different as capec:AttackPattern and cis:Control. Framework-specific subproperties (e.g. capec:attackTechniqueId, cis:mitigatesTechniqueId) carry the concrete literal. Retained after materialization — it records the source string as ingested, distinct from the resolved object-property edge."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTo",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Shortcut triple: generic relationship. Corresponds to STIX relationship_type 'related-to'."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "relatedTo"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reliability",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid254"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The assessed reliability of the source (e.g. using the NATO Admiralty Code A–F)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "reliability"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#remediates",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid202"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates an entity that addresses or corrects a Vulnerability or Weakness to the condition it remediates."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "remediates"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reportedBy",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid205"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a Report or Sighting to the Agent who created it."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "reportedBy"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reportedIn",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Vulnerability"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Publication"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A Vulnerability is formally disclosed in this Publication (advisory, CVE NVD entry, security bulletin). Primary arc into the Publication class."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "reportedIn"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resolvedTo",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Domain"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#IPAddress"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resolvesTo"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A Domain resolves to this IPAddress via DNS. More specific than stonework:resolvesTo (Infrastructure → Infrastructure); use this for explicit domain-to-IP mappings."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "resolvedTo"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resolvesTo",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Infrastructure"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Infrastructure"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates one Infrastructure entity to another Infrastructure entity to which it resolves, such as a Domain resolving to an IPAddress."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "resolvesTo"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelClub",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ResourceLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Resources typical of a small, informally organized group."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "club"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Club"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelContest",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ResourceLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Resources assembled temporarily for a competition or challenge."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "contest"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Contest"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelGovernment",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ResourceLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Resources comparable to those available to a national government."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "government"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Government"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelIndividual",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ResourceLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Resources available to a single person."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "individual"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Individual"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelOrganization",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ResourceLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Resources available to a sustained formal organization."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "organization"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Organization"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelScheme",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://docs.oasis-open.org/cti/stix/v2.1/os/stix-v2.1-os.html"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Resource Level Scheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The ordinal controlled vocabulary of organizational resources available to a threat actor."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Resource Level Scheme"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelTeam",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ResourceLevel"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Resources available to a coordinated operational team."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#resourceLevelScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "team"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Team"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#respondsToActivity",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialTransaction"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberActivity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A cyber activity whose occurrence prompted or provides the context for this financial transaction, without asserting that the transaction financed the activity."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "respondsToActivity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Use for a victim's ransom payment linked to the incident it responds to, restitution or remediation payments, and similar contextual relationships. Use stonework:fundsActivity only when the transaction finances the linked activity."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reviewFindingNotRelevant",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ReviewFinding"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The records were examined and do not bear on the investigation. They are not judged false or benign, only not relevant to it."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reviewFindingScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "not-relevant"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Not Relevant"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reviewFindingRelevant",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ReviewFinding"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The records bear on the investigation and are kept for analysis."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reviewFindingScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation" : [ {
    "@value" : "relevant"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relevant"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#reviewFindingScheme",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categoryScheme"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Review Finding Scheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The controlled vocabulary of what a review of records found."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "STONEWORK Review Finding Scheme"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#revisionOf",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Plan"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Plan"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasRevisionOf"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Relates a Plan to the earlier version of the same plan it revises."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "revisionOf"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Each version of a plan is its own Plan individual, with its stonework:planVersion, and a run is checked against the version it is stonework:executionOf. Once a Plan has runs, change it by making a revision rather than editing it: an edit in place would have past runs judged against a process they never followed. A Plan with no runs can be edited. Not transitive: the chain of versions is followed in a query, so withdrawing one link withdraws nothing else. After PROV-O's wasRevisionOf. A Plan adapted from a template stonework:implements the template instead: it is a realization, not a version."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#revokedBy",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Shortcut triple: source STIX object is revoked and superseded by target. Corresponds to STIX relationship_type 'revoked-by'."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "revokedBy"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#riskLevelCritical",
